('0ff0a716-6d87-50c1-bcf7-98ca8cb4b04e','1411a1f5-c0b5-54ea-9bfe-a3361c72a324',1,'difference','تفاوت','spoken & written','a clear difference or separation between two similar things','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'تمایز، تفاوت؛ تفکیک؛ درجه (عالی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a distinction ( also draw a distinction formal ) (= say or show that one exists ) It isn’t easy to make a distinction between these two words.','blur the distinction between something and something (= make it less clear ) Both sides in the war had been blurring the distinction between military and civilian targets.','see a distinction (= recognize that one exists ) He saw no distinction between religious beliefs and superstition.','a clear distinction The legal system makes a clear distinction between adults and children.','a fine/subtle distinction (= small ) Language enables us to make fine distinctions between similar ideas.','a sharp distinction (= very clear ) The president drew a sharp distinction between his party and the Republican Party.','an important/crucial distinction There is an important distinction between these two types of cancer.','a fundamental distinction (= a basic one ) There is a fundamental distinction between authors and readers.','a useful distinction He makes a useful distinction between the two theories.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the distinction between formal and informal language","translation":"تمایز بین زبان رسمی و غیر رسمی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000808507.mp3"},{"sentence":"There is often no clear distinction between an allergy and food intolerance.","translation":"اغلب هیچ تمایز واضحی بین آلرژی و عدم تحمل غذایی وجود ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001690358.mp3"},{"sentence":"The Act makes no distinction between children and adults (= it treats them as if they were the same ) .","translation":"این قانون هیچ تمایزی بین کودکان و بزرگسالان قائل نیست (= با آنها به گونه ای رفتار می کند که انگار آنها یکسان هستند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001690361.mp3"},{"sentence":"The law draws a distinction between temporary and permanent employees.","translation":"قانون بین کارمندان موقت و دائم تمایز قائل شده است.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,4),
('5cdb01a4-f573-535f-95b9-d886e8ca8540','1411a1f5-c0b5-54ea-9bfe-a3361c72a324',2,'excellence','تعالی','spoken & written','the quality of being excellent and important','[ uncountable ]',null,'کیفیت عالی و مهم بودن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a distinction ( also draw a distinction formal ) (= say or show that one exists ) It isn’t easy to make a distinction between these two words.','blur the distinction between something and something (= make it less clear ) Both sides in the war had been blurring the distinction between military and civilian targets.','see a distinction (= recognize that one exists ) He saw no distinction between religious beliefs and superstition.','a clear distinction The legal system makes a clear distinction between adults and children.','a fine/subtle distinction (= small ) Language enables us to make fine distinctions between similar ideas.','a sharp distinction (= very clear ) The president drew a sharp distinction between his party and the Republican Party.','an important/crucial distinction There is an important distinction between these two types of cancer.','a fundamental distinction (= a basic one ) There is a fundamental distinction between authors and readers.','a useful distinction He makes a useful distinction between the two theories.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Eliot’s distinction as a poet","translation":"تمایز الیوت به عنوان یک شاعر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000808517.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('028fc705-c069-5adb-83ea-746329cb564b','1411a1f5-c0b5-54ea-9bfe-a3361c72a324',3,'being special','خاص بودن','spoken & written','the quality of being special in some way','[ singular ]',null,'کیفیت خاص بودن به نوعی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a distinction ( also draw a distinction formal ) (= say or show that one exists ) It isn’t easy to make a distinction between these two words.','blur the distinction between something and something (= make it less clear ) Both sides in the war had been blurring the distinction between military and civilian targets.','see a distinction (= recognize that one exists ) He saw no distinction between religious beliefs and superstition.','a clear distinction The legal system makes a clear distinction between adults and children.','a fine/subtle distinction (= small ) Language enables us to make fine distinctions between similar ideas.','a sharp distinction (= very clear ) The president drew a sharp distinction between his party and the Republican Party.','an important/crucial distinction There is an important distinction between these two types of cancer.','a fundamental distinction (= a basic one ) There is a fundamental distinction between authors and readers.','a useful distinction He makes a useful distinction between the two theories.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"At that time, it had the distinction of being the largest bridge in the UK.","translation":"در آن زمان، این وجه تمایز به عنوان بزرگترین پل در بریتانیا بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001690369.mp3"},{"sentence":"The US enjoys the dubious distinction of being the lawsuit capital of the world.","translation":"ایالات متحده از تمایز مشکوک به عنوان پایتخت شکایت در جهان برخوردار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001690370.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
