('7a241c67-bad2-5065-9fe7-4075827acc0f','abbdb223-0d49-5a18-8930-c145172dec8f',2,null,null,'spoken & written','teaching you something you did not know before',null,null,'چیزی را به شما یاد می دهد که قبلاً نمی دانستید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"educational games","translation":"بازی های آموزشی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001181734.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('e1b057b1-3987-5c65-9c1e-3e794f54a16f','0601150c-2e3f-54c3-8485-96451e74fabe',1,null,null,'spoken & written','in a way that produces the result that was intended',null,null,'به‌طور مؤثر؛ در واقع، عملاً','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Children have to learn to communicate effectively.","translation":"کودکان باید یاد بگیرند که به طور موثر ارتباط برقرار کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001182122.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('5cac48c0-eaab-5f15-a4cd-f0f04332a0e1','0601150c-2e3f-54c3-8485-96451e74fabe',2,null,null,'spoken & written','used to describe what you see as the real facts of the situation','[ sentence adverb ]',null,'برای توصیف آنچه شما به عنوان حقایق واقعی وضعیت می بینید استفاده می شود',array['in effect']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Effectively, it has become impossible for us to help.","translation":"عملاً کمک کردن برای ما غیرممکن شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001182127.mp3"},{"sentence":"Most of the urban poor are effectively excluded from politics.","translation":"اکثر فقرای شهری عملاً از سیاست طرد شده اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001637496.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('2994f779-c7e8-58b2-a234-8b096b78d664','28839317-27f0-5424-9cc8-ff89c4814af8',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the power that is carried by wires , cable s etc, and is used to provide light or heat , to make machines work etc',null,null,'برق، الکتریسیته؛ هیجان (هوا)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['generate/produce electricity We need to find cleaner ways of generating electricity.','provide/supply electricity (= produce electricity and make it available to people ) The dam will provide water and electricity for 30 million people.','use electricity The system uses electricity to heat the water.','be powered by electricity In an emergency, the hospital can be powered by electricity from a generator.','conduct electricity (= used of a substance – allow electricity to travel along or through it ) Some metals conduct electricity better than others.','cut off the electricity (= stop the supply of electricity ) You risk having your electricity cut off if you fail to pay the bill.','the electricity supply (= electricity provided to homes and businesses ) The storms have disrupted the electricity supply to some areas.','electricity demand (= the amount of electricity that is needed ) There has been a dramatic growth in electricity demand.','electricity production (= the process of producing electricity, or the amount produced ) California’s strict environmental policies make it difficult to increase electricity production.','electricity consumption (= the amount of electricity that is used ) Our target is to cut electricity consumption by 10%.','an electricity bill (= a bill you have to pay for electricity you have used ) I pay my electricity bill by direct debit.','an electricity company Some electricity companies may be able to offer you an environmentally friendly option.','the electricity industry He works in the electricity industry.','mains electricity British English (= electricity supplied to a building from the national electricity supply ) The cottage has no mains electricity.','static electricity (= electricity that collects on a surface, for example on your clothes or a balloon ) He touched the door handle, and felt a jolt of static electricity.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The farm was very isolated, but it had electricity.","translation":"مزرعه بسیار منزوی بود، اما برق داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001183880.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('7e0d1e11-b68b-5936-ac26-5074056de199','28839317-27f0-5424-9cc8-ff89c4814af8',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a feeling of excitement',null,null,'یک احساس هیجان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['generate/produce electricity We need to find cleaner ways of generating electricity.','provide/supply electricity (= produce electricity and make it available to people ) The dam will provide water and electricity for 30 million people.','use electricity The system uses electricity to heat the water.','be powered by electricity In an emergency, the hospital can be powered by electricity from a generator.','conduct electricity (= used of a substance – allow electricity to travel along or through it ) Some metals conduct electricity better than others.','cut off the electricity (= stop the supply of electricity ) You risk having your electricity cut off if you fail to pay the bill.','the electricity supply (= electricity provided to homes and businesses ) The storms have disrupted the electricity supply to some areas.','electricity demand (= the amount of electricity that is needed ) There has been a dramatic growth in electricity demand.','electricity production (= the process of producing electricity, or the amount produced ) California’s strict environmental policies make it difficult to increase electricity production.','electricity consumption (= the amount of electricity that is used ) Our target is to cut electricity consumption by 10%.','an electricity bill (= a bill you have to pay for electricity you have used ) I pay my electricity bill by direct debit.','an electricity company Some electricity companies may be able to offer you an environmentally friendly option.','the electricity industry He works in the electricity industry.','mains electricity British English (= electricity supplied to a building from the national electricity supply ) The cottage has no mains electricity.','static electricity (= electricity that collects on a surface, for example on your clothes or a balloon ) He touched the door handle, and felt a jolt of static electricity.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There was electricity in the air between the two of them.","translation":"بین این دو نفر برق در هوا بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000512.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('3bd3efea-caa3-5dc2-b58d-8131a17fa6ac','d3dde113-967a-574f-9573-4af7c3093491',1,null,null,'spoken & written','feeling uncomfortable or nervous and worrying about what people think of you, for example because you have made a silly mistake , or because you have to talk or sing in public',null,null,'خجالت‌زده، دست‌پاچه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['terribly/deeply embarrassed (= very embarrassed ) I was deeply embarrassed to see my mother arrive in a very short skirt.','acutely/highly embarrassed (= extremely embarrassed ) The government must be acutely embarrassed by the minister’s behaviour.','slightly/a little embarrassed Tom looked slightly embarrassed when his name was called out.','somewhat embarrassed (= slightly embarrassed ) His family seemed somewhat embarrassed to be there.','clearly/obviously embarrassed (= in a way that is obvious to other people ) He was clearly embarrassed about what had happened.','feel embarrassed I felt embarrassed that he had seen me cry.','seem/look/sound embarrassed The judge seemed embarrassed to be asking her such personal questions.','get/become embarrassed Sometimes I get embarrassed, and I start to stutter.','an embarrassed silence There was an embarrassed silence, then Gina laughed loudly.','an embarrassed smile/laugh/grin Lucy gave an embarrassed smile and looked down at her feet.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Lori gets embarrassed if we ask her to sing.","translation":"اگر از او بخواهیم آواز بخواند، لری خجالت می کشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645827.mp3"},{"sentence":"He looked embarrassed when I asked him where he’d been.","translation":"وقتی از او پرسیدم کجا بوده، خجالت زده به نظر می رسید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645831.mp3"},{"sentence":"Michelle was acutely embarrassed (= very embarrassed ) at having to ask for money.","translation":"میشل از اینکه مجبور شد پول بخواهد به شدت خجالت زده بود (= بسیار خجالت زده بود).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645835.mp3"},{"sentence":"Ken gave her an embarrassed grin.","translation":"کن پوزخند خجالتی به او زد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645841.mp3"},{"sentence":"There was an embarrassed silence.","translation":"سکوت شرم آور حاکم شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001831866.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was embarrassed to admit making a mistake.","translation":"او از اعتراف به اشتباه خجالت می کشید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645844.mp3"},{"sentence":"I felt embarrassed about how untidy the house was.","translation":"از اینکه خانه چقدر نامرتب است احساس شرمندگی می کردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001185484.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('e6303e37-a235-569a-b6ec-c3829eee5e52','d3dde113-967a-574f-9573-4af7c3093491',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'financially embarrassed','خجالت‌زده، دست‌پاچه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['terribly/deeply embarrassed (= very embarrassed ) I was deeply embarrassed to see my mother arrive in a very short skirt.','acutely/highly embarrassed (= extremely embarrassed ) The government must be acutely embarrassed by the minister’s behaviour.','slightly/a little embarrassed Tom looked slightly embarrassed when his name was called out.','somewhat embarrassed (= slightly embarrassed ) His family seemed somewhat embarrassed to be there.','clearly/obviously embarrassed (= in a way that is obvious to other people ) He was clearly embarrassed about what had happened.','feel embarrassed I felt embarrassed that he had seen me cry.','seem/look/sound embarrassed The judge seemed embarrassed to be asking her such personal questions.','get/become embarrassed Sometimes I get embarrassed, and I start to stutter.','an embarrassed silence There was an embarrassed silence, then Gina laughed loudly.','an embarrassed smile/laugh/grin Lucy gave an embarrassed smile and looked down at her feet.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('b774cfbc-3814-5425-86e3-858bb337de84','67fb2fe8-88a6-5e02-a413-31ec572b0362',1,null,null,'spoken & written','giving you hope and confidence',null,null,'امیدبخش، دلگرم‌کننده',array['reassuring']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The encouraging news is that typhoid is on the decrease.","translation":"خبر دلگرم کننده این است که تیفوس در حال کاهش است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001677919.mp3"},{"sentence":"The signs are encouraging — but there’s a long way to go.","translation":"نشانه ها دلگرم کننده هستند - اما راه زیادی در پیش است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001677923.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('8e600cbc-d7bc-57e3-8eb9-7ad8059862ae','ce9e903a-671b-58fd-a0cf-16061e15a42d',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the work involved in designing and building roads , bridges , machines etc',null,null,'مهندسی، فنی؛ مهارت مهندسی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('b82578de-fa47-5ca9-8346-9fe878961fc0','16350373-2d4e-56b3-a6c3-78c86b6ee395',1,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'the environment','محیط، اطراف؛ محیط زیست؛ کارگاه (رایانه)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['protect the environment We need to take drastic steps to protect the environment.','conserve the environment formal (= protect it and prevent it from changing or being damaged ) People need to live in harmony with nature and conserve the environment.','harm/damage the environment The government insists that the dam will not harm the environment.','destroy the environment We need to find ways of producing energy without destroying the environment.','pollute the environment Nuclear waste will pollute the environment for centuries.','clean up the environment It’s about time that we started cleaning up the environment.','the natural environment Current methods of farming are damaging the natural environment.','the marine environment (= the sea and the creatures that live there ) Fish farming poses a threat to the marine environment.','be good/bad for the environment Plastic bags are bad for the environment.','be harmful to the environment Emissions from cars are harmful to the environment.','protection of the environment In developing countries, protection of the environment is not a primary concern.','conservation of the environment There are many organizations dedicated to conservation of the environment.','damage/harm to the environment A lot of chemicals used in industry cause harm to the environment.','the destruction of the environment Logging has led to the destruction of the natural environment.','pollution of the environment The waste material must be stored safely to avoid pollution of the environment.','the effect/impact on the environment The building’s design will minimize its impact on the environment.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('e1c2cccc-4fb2-505b-a935-fdd28d1883e3','16350373-2d4e-56b3-a6c3-78c86b6ee395',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the people and things that are around you in your life, for example the buildings you use, the people you live or work with, and the general situation you are in','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'افراد و چیزهایی که در زندگی شما در اطراف شما هستند، به عنوان مثال ساختمان هایی که استفاده می کنید، افرادی که با آنها زندگی می کنید یا کار می کنید، و وضعیت کلی که در آن هستید.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The company had failed to provide a safe environment for its workers.","translation":"این شرکت نتوانسته بود محیطی امن برای کارگران خود فراهم کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001642057.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('b990e5e5-ffd6-5bc7-8540-595b41005c7e','16350373-2d4e-56b3-a6c3-78c86b6ee395',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the natural features of a place, for example its weather , the type of land it has, and the type of plants that grow in it','[ countable ]',null,'ویژگی های طبیعی یک مکان، به عنوان مثال آب و هوا، نوع زمین آن، و نوع گیاهانی که در آن رشد می کنند.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a forest environment","translation":"یک محیط جنگلی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001642071.mp3"},{"sentence":"a very adaptable creature that will eat different foods in different environments","translation":"موجودی بسیار سازگار که در محیط های مختلف غذاهای مختلفی می خورد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001642072.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('ccf105db-ed02-5ccc-b343-3aa8d6ebfcd7','6c8a971a-bddb-5dd4-b939-0d464d14f15d',1,null,null,'spoken & written','used when stating the most basic facts about something','[ sentence adverb ]',null,'ذاتاً، بنیاداً؛ اساساً (خلاصه)',array['basically']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Ballet is essentially a middle-class interest.","translation":"باله اساساً یک علاقه طبقه متوسط ​​است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001614569.mp3"},{"sentence":"Suicide rates have remained essentially unchanged.","translation":"نرخ خودکشی اساساً بدون تغییر باقی مانده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001614570.mp3"},{"sentence":"Essentially, we are talking about the cold war period.","translation":"اساساً ما در مورد دوران جنگ سرد صحبت می کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001219225.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('a0271195-5c85-54fc-90a2-0b5f7edd3835','0d363472-5085-5055-addf-734d316e0659',1,null,null,'formal','a spoken or written test of knowledge , especially an important one','[ countable ]',null,'امتحان، آزمون؛ معاینه (پزشکی)؛ بررسی دقیق',array['exam']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['take an examination ( also sit an examination British English ) Do you have to take an examination in every subject?','pass an examination (= succeed in it ) I really hope that Suzie passes the examination.','fail an examination Michael had never yet failed an examination.','study for an examination ( also revise for an examination British English ) I have been studying all week for the examination.','do well/badly in an examination He did well in his examinations, and went on to study at MIT.','cheat in an examination Any student caught cheating in an examination will be suspended.','a final examination (= at the end of a course ) My final examinations take place in June.','a written/oral examination For French, there is an oral and a written examination.','a chemistry/French etc examination Most of the pupils passed their science examination with flying colours.','an entrance examination (= to enter a school or university ) He had now failed the college entrance examination twice.','a mock examination (= a practice examination to prepare for the real one ) Mock examinations help you to prepare for the real thing.','A-level/high school etc examinations The school usually achieves good results in GCSE examinations.','examination results You will receive your examination results in the post.','an examination paper There will be a choice of questions on the examination paper.','an examination question Read the examination questions carefully before writing your answers.','examination revision I need to find somewhere quiet to do some examination revision.','an examination script (= everything that someone writes in an examination ) I''ve just finished marking 200 examination scripts.','examination marks On average, girls achieved higher examination marks that boys.','an examination pass To apply, you need at least two A-level examination passes.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The examination results will be announced in September.","translation":"نتایج آزمون شهریور ماه اعلام خواهد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001224440.mp3"},{"sentence":"He’s already taken the entrance examination .","translation":"او قبلاً در آزمون ورودی شرکت کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001734864.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('13b032de-1457-5788-8674-90fae9533500','0d363472-5085-5055-addf-734d316e0659',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the process of looking at something carefully in order to see what it is like','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'فرآیند نگاه کردن به چیزی با دقت به منظور دیدن اینکه چگونه است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a detailed examination of population statistics","translation":"بررسی دقیق آمار جمعیت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001224445.mp3"},{"sentence":"The proposals are still under examination.","translation":"پیشنهادات هنوز در دست بررسی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001734875.mp3"},{"sentence":"The issues need further examination .","translation":"مسائل نیاز به بررسی بیشتر دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001734876.mp3"},{"sentence":"On closer examination the vases were seen to be cracked.","translation":"در بررسی دقیق تر گلدان ها ترک خورده بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001224451.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('b85ca6ac-e8ae-5b73-85a9-4db7a094032f','0d363472-5085-5055-addf-734d316e0659',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a set of medical tests','[ countable ]',null,'مجموعه ای از آزمایشات پزشکی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"All patients had a complete physical examination.","translation":"همه بیماران تحت معاینه فیزیکی کامل قرار گرفتند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001734882.mp3"},{"sentence":"A post-mortem examination (= an examination on a dead body ) showed that he died from head injuries.","translation":"معاینه پس از مرگ (= معاینه جسد مرده) نشان داد که او بر اثر جراحات به سر فوت کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001734883.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('a5434fa6-028f-5817-ab5b-1e83b83b35fd','0d363472-5085-5055-addf-734d316e0659',4,null,null,'law','the process of asking questions to get specific information, especially in a court of law','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'فرآیند پرسیدن سؤال برای به دست آوردن اطلاعات خاص، به ویژه در دادگاه حقوقی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('883984fc-26fe-5ccf-a36c-290d6ea585d1','22eaae43-cb82-599d-b5a4-bbfad4869b04',1,null,null,'spoken & written','what you think or hope will happen','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'انتظار، چشم‌داشت؛ توقع','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['high (= expecting that someone or something will be successful ) Like most parents, we have high expectations for our children.','low (= expecting that someone or something will not be very successful ) Their expectations of success were pretty low.','great expectations (= very high ) Emigrants sailed to America with great expectations.','reasonable expectations (= the expectation that something will probably be successful, but may not be ) It is a difficult operation, but we have reasonable expectations of success.','realistic expectations (= the expectation that bad things can happen as well as good things ) The disease is not curable, and patients must have realistic expectations.','unreasonable/unrealistic expectations (= expectations that are too high ) I think you had unrealistic expectations of what could be achieved in the time.','legitimate expectations law (= expectations based on someone''s legal rights ) The men have legitimate expectations of a fair hearing.','growing/rising/increased expectations (= becoming higher ) China''s economy will grow considerably over the next five years, bringing rising expectations of wealth.','general/popular/widespread expectations (= shared by a lot of people ) The general expectation was for married couples to have children.','family/parental expectations (= expectations that families or parents have for their children ) Parental expectations for a first child tend to be quite high.','social expectations (= relating to what society thinks or expects ) Social expectations of masculine and feminine behaviour changed drastically during the 1960s and ''70s.','career expectations (= someone''s expectations about how well they will do in their job ) People with low self-esteem usually have low career expectations.','have expectations ( also hold expectations formal ) Many migrant workers had high expectations when they arrived, but not anymore.','raise somebody''s expectations (= make someone expect more success, money etc ) Having raised expectations, the government failed to live up to its promises.','lower somebody''s expectations (= make someone expect less success, money etc ) If you can''t afford your dream home, you may have to lower your expectations.','come up to/live up to somebody''s expectations (= be as good as someone hoped or expected ) The match was boring, and didn''t live up to our expectations at all.','fulfil/satisfy somebody''s expectations formal (= be as good as someone hoped or expected ) The band failed to fulfil the fans'' expectations.','exceed/surpass somebody''s expectations (= be or do better than you hoped or expected ) The holiday exceeded our expectations.','fall below/fall short of somebody''s expectations (= be worse that someone hoped or expected ) Our profits last year fell below expectations.','create expectations (= make people expect that something will happen ) The events of the last few weeks have created expectations of an economic recession.','confound somebody''s expectations (= be different to what someone expected, in a way that surprises or confuses them ) The play totally confounds the audience''s expectations.','above expectations (= higher, better, or more successful than expected ) Economic growth last month was above expectations.','below expectations (= lower, worse, or less successful than expected ) Retail sales in December were well below expectations.','beyond all expectations (= greater or better than someone expected ) The task took two months to complete, but it was successful far beyond all expectations.','against/contrary to expectations (= very different to what someone expected ) Contrary to our expectations, the share price actually increased.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"For some time he lived with the expectation that he was going to die.","translation":"مدتی با این انتظار زندگی کرد که قرار است بمیرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001232856.mp3"},{"sentence":"Anne left Germany in the expectation of seeing her family again before very long.","translation":"آن آلمان را ترک کرد به این امید که قبل از مدت ها دوباره خانواده اش را ببیند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001232863.mp3"},{"sentence":"Against all expectations, getting up at five is actually easier in winter.","translation":"برخلاف تمام انتظارات، بیدار شدن در ساعت پنج در زمستان آسان‌تر است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001232859.mp3"},{"sentence":"Having raised expectations (= made people more hopeful ) , he went on to help only a few people.","translation":"او با افزایش توقعات (= مردم را امیدوارتر کرد)، تنها به چند نفر کمک کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653694.mp3"},{"sentence":"Profits are below expectations.","translation":"سود کمتر از حد انتظار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653701.mp3"},{"sentence":"Gina has succeeded beyond our expectations.","translation":"جینا فراتر از انتظارات ما موفق بوده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001232875.mp3"},{"sentence":"The show exceeded all expectations (= was much better than expected ) .","translation":"نمایش فراتر از همه انتظارات بود (= خیلی بهتر از حد انتظار بود).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653704.mp3"},{"sentence":"His performance did not live up to our expectations (= was not as good as we expected ) .","translation":"عملکرد او انتظارات ما را برآورده نکرد (= آنطور که انتظار داشتیم خوب نبود).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653711.mp3"},{"sentence":"The number of people who attended fell short of expectations (= was lower than expected ) .","translation":"تعداد افرادی که شرکت کردند کمتر از حد انتظار بود (= کمتر از حد انتظار بود).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653713.mp3"}]'::jsonb,9),
('52bc78a6-1fc2-56a6-9666-5f1a45e358a4','22eaae43-cb82-599d-b5a4-bbfad4869b04',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a feeling or belief about the way something should be or how someone should behave','[ countable usually plural ]',null,'یک احساس یا باور در مورد اینکه چیزی باید چگونه باشد یا اینکه یک نفر چگونه باید رفتار کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['high (= expecting that someone or something will be successful ) Like most parents, we have high expectations for our children.','low (= expecting that someone or something will not be very successful ) Their expectations of success were pretty low.','great expectations (= very high ) Emigrants sailed to America with great expectations.','reasonable expectations (= the expectation that something will probably be successful, but may not be ) It is a difficult operation, but we have reasonable expectations of success.','realistic expectations (= the expectation that bad things can happen as well as good things ) The disease is not curable, and patients must have realistic expectations.','unreasonable/unrealistic expectations (= expectations that are too high ) I think you had unrealistic expectations of what could be achieved in the time.','legitimate expectations law (= expectations based on someone''s legal rights ) The men have legitimate expectations of a fair hearing.','growing/rising/increased expectations (= becoming higher ) China''s economy will grow considerably over the next five years, bringing rising expectations of wealth.','general/popular/widespread expectations (= shared by a lot of people ) The general expectation was for married couples to have children.','family/parental expectations (= expectations that families or parents have for their children ) Parental expectations for a first child tend to be quite high.','social expectations (= relating to what society thinks or expects ) Social expectations of masculine and feminine behaviour changed drastically during the 1960s and ''70s.','career expectations (= someone''s expectations about how well they will do in their job ) People with low self-esteem usually have low career expectations.','have expectations ( also hold expectations formal ) Many migrant workers had high expectations when they arrived, but not anymore.','raise somebody''s expectations (= make someone expect more success, money etc ) Having raised expectations, the government failed to live up to its promises.','lower somebody''s expectations (= make someone expect less success, money etc ) If you can''t afford your dream home, you may have to lower your expectations.','come up to/live up to somebody''s expectations (= be as good as someone hoped or expected ) The match was boring, and didn''t live up to our expectations at all.','fulfil/satisfy somebody''s expectations formal (= be as good as someone hoped or expected ) The band failed to fulfil the fans'' expectations.','exceed/surpass somebody''s expectations (= be or do better than you hoped or expected ) The holiday exceeded our expectations.','fall below/fall short of somebody''s expectations (= be worse that someone hoped or expected ) Our profits last year fell below expectations.','create expectations (= make people expect that something will happen ) The events of the last few weeks have created expectations of an economic recession.','confound somebody''s expectations (= be different to what someone expected, in a way that surprises or confuses them ) The play totally confounds the audience''s expectations.','above expectations (= higher, better, or more successful than expected ) Economic growth last month was above expectations.','below expectations (= lower, worse, or less successful than expected ) Retail sales in December were well below expectations.','beyond all expectations (= greater or better than someone expected ) The task took two months to complete, but it was successful far beyond all expectations.','against/contrary to expectations (= very different to what someone expected ) Contrary to our expectations, the share price actually increased.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Women who have high expectations of marriage are often disappointed.","translation":"زنانی که انتظارات زیادی از ازدواج دارند اغلب ناامید می شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653720.mp3"},{"sentence":"Some people have totally unrealistic expectations of both medical and nursing staff.","translation":"برخی از مردم انتظارات کاملاً غیر واقعی هم از کادر پزشکی و هم از کادر پرستاری دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001232892.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('e5c13e37-dcf6-590f-95ac-4bd4db140f4a','22eaae43-cb82-599d-b5a4-bbfad4869b04',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'expectation of life','انتظار، چشم‌داشت؛ توقع','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('e5b55f4e-f2ee-5ee9-bfcb-b6536fe1661f','116c756d-c7d3-5740-beda-756e4b2ea91c',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the total amount of money that a government, organization , or person spends during a particular period of time','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'هزینه، مصارف (مجموع)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['public/government/state expenditure (= money a government spends on the services it provides for people ) The Conservatives want to maintain a firm control on public expenditure.','national/local expenditure (= money spent by national or local government ) There have been cuts in local expenditure on education.','military/defence expenditure (= money that a government spends on the armed forces ) Military expenditure has been growing year on year.','health/welfare/education expenditure (= money that a government spends on providing health services, welfare, or education ) There has been a steady rise in welfare expenditure.','household expenditure (= the amount of money the people in a house spend on food, heating etc ) Sally cut her household expenditure and tried to save every penny she could.','total/overall expenditure The company''s total expenditure rose by 19%.','additional/extra expenditure Businesses have been forced to pass on the additional expenditure to customers.','capital expenditure (= money that a company spends on buildings, machinery etc ) Capital expenditure on IT equipment will come from a different budget.','gross/net expenditure (= the total amount a company spends before/after any tax or costs have been taken away ) Spending on research and development represents 13% of our gross expenditure.','increase expenditure The company plans to increase capital expenditure by 20% this financial year.','cut/reduce expenditure Their policies are designed to cut public expenditure.','expenditure rises As public expenditure has risen, so have taxes.','expenditure falls Government expenditure on scientific research has fallen in the last few years.','an increase/rise in expenditure The government has announced a planned 4.4% increase in public expenditure.','a cut/reduction in expenditure There has been a marked reduction in expenditure on some social and welfare services.','an item of expenditure (= something a government or person spends money on ) Housing is the biggest single item of expenditure in the budgets of most households.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"expenditure on research and development","translation":"هزینه های تحقیق و توسعه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001233138.mp3"},{"sentence":"huge cuts in public expenditure (= the amount of money a government spends on services for the public )","translation":"کاهش عظیم در هزینه های عمومی (= مقدار پولی که دولت برای خدمات عمومی خرج می کند)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653766.mp3"},{"sentence":"government expenditure on education","translation":"هزینه های دولت برای آموزش","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653770.mp3"},{"sentence":"capital expenditure (= spending by a company on buildings, machinery, equipment etc )","translation":"مخارج سرمایه ای (= هزینه های یک شرکت برای ساختمان ها، ماشین آلات، تجهیزات و غیره)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001233135.mp3"},{"sentence":"an expenditure of £1 million","translation":"هزینه ای بالغ بر 1 میلیون پوند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653776.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('a5a8be89-fa25-5fc2-af46-6c9d74c2c138','116c756d-c7d3-5740-beda-756e4b2ea91c',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the action of spending or using time, money, energy etc','[ uncountable ]',null,'عمل صرف یا استفاده از زمان، پول، انرژی و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['public/government/state expenditure (= money a government spends on the services it provides for people ) The Conservatives want to maintain a firm control on public expenditure.','national/local expenditure (= money spent by national or local government ) There have been cuts in local expenditure on education.','military/defence expenditure (= money that a government spends on the armed forces ) Military expenditure has been growing year on year.','health/welfare/education expenditure (= money that a government spends on providing health services, welfare, or education ) There has been a steady rise in welfare expenditure.','household expenditure (= the amount of money the people in a house spend on food, heating etc ) Sally cut her household expenditure and tried to save every penny she could.','total/overall expenditure The company''s total expenditure rose by 19%.','additional/extra expenditure Businesses have been forced to pass on the additional expenditure to customers.','capital expenditure (= money that a company spends on buildings, machinery etc ) Capital expenditure on IT equipment will come from a different budget.','gross/net expenditure (= the total amount a company spends before/after any tax or costs have been taken away ) Spending on research and development represents 13% of our gross expenditure.','increase expenditure The company plans to increase capital expenditure by 20% this financial year.','cut/reduce expenditure Their policies are designed to cut public expenditure.','expenditure rises As public expenditure has risen, so have taxes.','expenditure falls Government expenditure on scientific research has fallen in the last few years.','an increase/rise in expenditure The government has announced a planned 4.4% increase in public expenditure.','a cut/reduction in expenditure There has been a marked reduction in expenditure on some social and welfare services.','an item of expenditure (= something a government or person spends money on ) Housing is the biggest single item of expenditure in the budgets of most households.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the expenditure of time and money on your house or garden","translation":"صرف زمان و پول برای خانه یا باغ شما","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001233151.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('e91cb4db-546d-5890-8acd-983931d43993','13dd13fa-d211-5e77-87da-8e7821fd357a',1,null,null,'spoken & written','possessing skills or knowledge because you have done something often or for a long time',null,null,'باتجربه، کارآزموده','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"an experienced pilot","translation":"یک خلبان با تجربه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001233854.mp3"},{"sentence":"an experienced public speaker","translation":"یک سخنران عمومی با تجربه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653859.mp3"},{"sentence":"She is experienced and self-assured.","translation":"او با تجربه و مطمئن است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653860.mp3"},{"sentence":"Blake’s very experienced in microsurgery.","translation":"بلیک در جراحی میکروسکوپی بسیار مجرب است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001233857.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('ec941edd-f9b9-5782-a39a-d575cce5798c','53f0b840-c995-5e84-a233-aaa5613af087',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the reasons you give for why something happened or why you did something','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'توضیح، شرح؛ توجیه (دلیل)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have an explanation Does the hospital have any explanation for why he died?','give an explanation The police gave no explanation for their actions.','provide/offer an explanation This theory may provide an explanation for the origins of the universe.','ask for/demand an explanation When I asked for an explanation, the people at the office said they didn''t know. Furious parents are demanding an explanation from the school.','wait for an explanation (= expect an explanation ) She continued to stare at him in silence, waiting for an explanation.','find/think of/come up with an explanation Scientists have been unable to find an explanation for this phenomenon.','owe (somebody) an explanation I think you owe me some kind of explanation.','accept an explanation (= believe that it is true or correct ) The court accepted her explanation.','need/require an explanation We think the minister’s decision requires an explanation.','a possible explanation Can anyone think of a possible explanation for why this is happening?','the most likely/probable explanation (= one that is probably true ) The most likely explanation is that John missed the bus. The most probable explanation is that the water was contaminated.','an obvious explanation (= one that is easy to see or notice ) There is no obvious explanation for his strange behaviour.','a reasonable/plausible explanation (= one that is easy to believe ) Pilot error is the most plausible explanation for the crash.','a satisfactory/adequate explanation (= one that explains something completely ) A bank must offer an adequate explanation of all its charges.','a convincing/credible explanation (= one that you can believe is true ) The author fails to provide a convincing explanation for the main character’s motives.','a logical/rational explanation (= one that is based on facts ) Physics finally gave us a rational explanation for the atom’s strange behaviour.','further explanation (= additional reasons ) He gave no further explanation for leaving, and she did not ask for any.','there is no apparent explanation (= used when there is no explanation that you can think of ) There was no apparent explanation for the attack.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Can you think of any explanation for this failure?","translation":"آیا می توانید توضیحی برای این شکست بیاندیشید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000542.mp3"},{"sentence":"The concert was cancelled without explanation.","translation":"کنسرت بدون توضیح لغو شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040060.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('720ac6d1-91c4-527b-8943-2f05850600b4','53f0b840-c995-5e84-a233-aaa5613af087',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a statement or piece of writing intended to describe how something works or make something easier to understand','[ countable ]',null,'بیانیه یا نوشته‌ای که برای توصیف نحوه کارکرد چیزی یا آسان‌تر کردن درک چیزی است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have an explanation Does the hospital have any explanation for why he died?','give an explanation The police gave no explanation for their actions.','provide/offer an explanation This theory may provide an explanation for the origins of the universe.','ask for/demand an explanation When I asked for an explanation, the people at the office said they didn''t know. Furious parents are demanding an explanation from the school.','wait for an explanation (= expect an explanation ) She continued to stare at him in silence, waiting for an explanation.','find/think of/come up with an explanation Scientists have been unable to find an explanation for this phenomenon.','owe (somebody) an explanation I think you owe me some kind of explanation.','accept an explanation (= believe that it is true or correct ) The court accepted her explanation.','need/require an explanation We think the minister’s decision requires an explanation.','a possible explanation Can anyone think of a possible explanation for why this is happening?','the most likely/probable explanation (= one that is probably true ) The most likely explanation is that John missed the bus. The most probable explanation is that the water was contaminated.','an obvious explanation (= one that is easy to see or notice ) There is no obvious explanation for his strange behaviour.','a reasonable/plausible explanation (= one that is easy to believe ) Pilot error is the most plausible explanation for the crash.','a satisfactory/adequate explanation (= one that explains something completely ) A bank must offer an adequate explanation of all its charges.','a convincing/credible explanation (= one that you can believe is true ) The author fails to provide a convincing explanation for the main character’s motives.','a logical/rational explanation (= one that is based on facts ) Physics finally gave us a rational explanation for the atom’s strange behaviour.','further explanation (= additional reasons ) He gave no further explanation for leaving, and she did not ask for any.','there is no apparent explanation (= used when there is no explanation that you can think of ) There was no apparent explanation for the attack.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The ability to give clear explanations is the most important quality of the ideal teacher.","translation":"توانایی ارائه توضیحات واضح مهمترین ویژگی معلم ایده آل است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001197209.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’ll try and give you a quick explanation of how the machine works.","translation":"سعی می کنم توضیح سریعی در مورد نحوه کار دستگاه به شما بدهم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001197212.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('64651041-ecbc-5632-8def-c2d8e2c971b0','2029be36-cfa0-5592-a768-2b35acdd642b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','extremely interesting',null,null,'دلربا، بسیار جالب','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a fascinating book","translation":"یک کتاب جذاب","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001212840.mp3"},{"sentence":"That sounds absolutely fascinating .","translation":"این کاملاً جذاب به نظر می رسد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001641880.mp3"},{"sentence":"I found him quite fascinating.","translation":"من او را بسیار جذاب یافتم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001212843.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('6530695e-478e-522c-a421-b406a32e7565','19050814-d6f3-5a89-a1b5-894ae60cc44e',1,null,null,'spoken & written','relating to the most basic and important parts of something',null,null,'بنیادی، اساسی، پایه‌ای','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a fundamental change A fundamental change is needed in the voting system.','a fundamental difference There is no fundamental difference between people of different races.','a fundamental distinction (= a clear difference between two similar things ) A fundamental distinction exists between knowing a fact and understanding it.','a fundamental problem Charity could not solve the fundamental problem of unemployment.','a fundamental question To reach a solution several fundamental questions need to be answered.','a fundamental issue This report raises a number of fundamental issues.','the fundamental reason The fundamental reason for the project’s failure was the lack of funds.','the fundamental cause A burst tyre was the fundamental cause of the crash.','a fundamental mistake/error The government made at least one fundamental mistake when drawing up this legislation.','a fundamental weakness (= fault ) She points out the fundamental weaknesses in his argument.','a fundamental flaw (= fault that makes something imperfect ) There is a fundamental flaw in the current tax system.','fundamental principles (= moral rules or beliefs about what is right and wrong ) Let me state a couple of fundamental principles which we value highly.','something is of fundamental importance (= it is extremely important ) It is of fundamental importance that justice should be seen to be done.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We have to tackle the fundamental cause of the problem.","translation":"ما باید با علت اساسی مشکل مقابله کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001315706.mp3"},{"sentence":"a fundamental difference in opinion","translation":"اختلاف نظر اساسی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001315709.mp3"},{"sentence":"Novice programmers sometimes make fundamental errors.","translation":"برنامه نویسان تازه کار گاهی اوقات اشتباهات اساسی مرتکب می شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001315712.mp3"},{"sentence":"the fundamental principles of liberty and equality","translation":"اصول اساسی آزادی و برابری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001824321.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('d2cdda32-381f-5530-a50d-11297a86e341','19050814-d6f3-5a89-a1b5-894ae60cc44e',2,null,null,'spoken & written','very necessary and important',null,null,'بسیار ضروری و مهم','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a fundamental change A fundamental change is needed in the voting system.','a fundamental difference There is no fundamental difference between people of different races.','a fundamental distinction (= a clear difference between two similar things ) A fundamental distinction exists between knowing a fact and understanding it.','a fundamental problem Charity could not solve the fundamental problem of unemployment.','a fundamental question To reach a solution several fundamental questions need to be answered.','a fundamental issue This report raises a number of fundamental issues.','the fundamental reason The fundamental reason for the project’s failure was the lack of funds.','the fundamental cause A burst tyre was the fundamental cause of the crash.','a fundamental mistake/error The government made at least one fundamental mistake when drawing up this legislation.','a fundamental weakness (= fault ) She points out the fundamental weaknesses in his argument.','a fundamental flaw (= fault that makes something imperfect ) There is a fundamental flaw in the current tax system.','fundamental principles (= moral rules or beliefs about what is right and wrong ) Let me state a couple of fundamental principles which we value highly.','something is of fundamental importance (= it is extremely important ) It is of fundamental importance that justice should be seen to be done.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"fundamental human rights","translation":"حقوق اساسی بشر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001824325.mp3"},{"sentence":"Water is fundamental to survival.","translation":"آب برای بقا ضروری است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001315718.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('39451c3d-193e-5879-916e-95dfa11a59f9','03ee1001-bf20-58c8-94ae-f08e09b671a5',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the father of your father or mother',null,null,'پدربزرگ','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I used to stay at my grandpa ’s house.","translation":"من در خانه پدربزرگم می ماندم.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,1),
('ebfe3ace-0975-552e-b158-c9cd7f57551d','5932a28c-28ca-545e-b058-ec0665c43302',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the mother of your mother or father',null,null,'مادربزرگ','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"My grandma used to make lovely cakes.","translation":"مادربزرگ من کیک های خوشمزه درست می کرد.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,1),
('e53a055e-b7e8-50e2-89fb-9c1cd7352a95','4d21d1a6-ce63-54fc-a64e-146319fe05ac',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the ability to form pictures or ideas in your mind','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'تخیل، قوه تصور؛ تصورات (زیبا)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a good imagination She''s a lively child, with a good imagination.','great imagination His paintings show great imagination.','a vivid/fertile imagination (= an ability to think of a lot of ideas and things that could happen ) She had a fertile imagination and a great sense of humour. With your vivid imagination, you should write a book.','an overactive/fevered imagination (= a mind that imagines strange things that are not real ) These stories are the product of an overactive imagination.','the public imagination The story captured the public imagination.','creative imagination I don''t have the creative imagination to be a writer.','have (an) imagination Her poems show that she has a lot of imagination.','use your imagination Musicians need to use their imagination as well as their technical skills.','show/display imagination His latest paintings display a vivid imagination.','lack imagination A lot of today''s pop music seems to lack imagination.','fire/stimulate somebody''s imagination (= make someone use their imagination ) The aim of the exhibition is to stimulate people''s imagination.','be full of imagination Her stories are full of imagination.','a lack of imagination Their policies show a lack of imagination.','let your imagination run wild ( also let your imagination run riot British English ) (= allow yourself to imagine many strange or wonderful things ) He uses painting as a way of letting his imagination run riot.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a storyteller with an incredible imagination","translation":"داستان نویسی با تخیل باورنکردنی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000820.mp3"},{"sentence":"It does not take much imagination to understand their grief.","translation":"برای درک غم و اندوه آنها تخیل زیادی لازم نیست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000821.mp3"},{"sentence":"With a little imagination, you can find great inexpensive gifts.","translation":"با کمی تخیل می توانید هدایای ارزان قیمت عالی پیدا کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000822.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
