('88adc09d-76dd-54e5-a996-7fd1b55b75c8','bbe9aded-d3a7-5c00-a379-a9d03d3b8f21',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the way in which two people or two groups feel about each other and behave towards each other','[ countable ]',null,'رابطه، پیوند (فرد)؛ رابطه (عاطفی)؛ رابطه (کار)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a relationship We’ve always had a good relationship with our neighbours.','develop/form/build a relationship By that age, children start developing relationships outside the family.','forge a relationship (= develop a strong relationship ) We want to forge closer relationships with our allies.','cement a relationship (= make it firm and strong ) We want to cement relationships with other transport associations.','make relationships I found it impossible to make new relationships.','good/great Over the years, we’ve developed a good relationship.','close Laura had a very close relationship with her grandmother.','friendly/harmonious My friendly relationship with Scott’s family continued after his death.','strong Our relationship is strong enough to survive anything.','a love-hate relationship (= when someone both likes and dislikes someone else ) The local people have a love-hate relationship with tourists.','a special relationship (= a particularly close relationship ) I did not want to risk losing this special relationship we shared.','a supportive relationship People lacking supportive relationships were expected to be prone to depression.','a working relationship (= a relationship appropriate for people who work together ) She’s a fine actress and we developed a great working relationship.','family relationships Travelling a lot for business can strain family relationships.','a personal relationship Drinking affects personal relationships.','human relationships Human relationships fascinate me.','a social relationship Satisfactory social relationships with adults are very important.','a business/professional relationship Both companies want to continue their business relationship into the future.','the doctor-patient/parent-child/teacher-student etc relationship A family crisis can adversely affect the developing parent-child relationship.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I have quite a good relationship with my parents.","translation":"من رابطه بسیار خوبی با پدر و مادرم دارم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001769355.mp3"},{"sentence":"the special relationship between Britain and the US","translation":"روابط ویژه بریتانیا و آمریکا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001769356.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('282ebcaa-3221-5392-84be-1b3f1e4949aa','bbe9aded-d3a7-5c00-a379-a9d03d3b8f21',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the way in which two or more things are connected and affect each other','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'روشی که در آن دو یا چند چیز به هم متصل می شوند و بر یکدیگر تأثیر می گذارند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the relationship between diet and health problems","translation":"رابطه بین رژیم غذایی و مشکلات سلامتی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001327.mp3"},{"sentence":"He’s studying politics and its relationship to the media.","translation":"او در حال مطالعه سیاست و رابطه آن با رسانه است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652678.mp3"},{"sentence":"The lessons bear little relationship to (= they are not connected to ) the children’s needs.","translation":"دروس ارتباط کمی با نیازهای کودکان دارند (= به آنها متصل نیستند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001328.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('448d4f9c-9134-5f3a-bf64-866c8d1067cd','bbe9aded-d3a7-5c00-a379-a9d03d3b8f21',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a situation in which two people spend time together or live together, and have romantic or sexual feelings for each other','[ countable ]',null,'موقعیتی که در آن دو نفر با هم وقت می گذرانند یا با هم زندگی می کنند و احساسات عاشقانه یا جنسی نسبت به یکدیگر دارند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He’s never had a sexual relationship before.","translation":"او قبلاً هرگز رابطه جنسی نداشته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652691.mp3"},{"sentence":"She doesn’t really want a relationship with me.","translation":"او واقعاً نمی خواهد با من رابطه داشته باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652686.mp3"},{"sentence":"Are you in a relationship right now?","translation":"آیا در حال حاضر در یک رابطه هستید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652687.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('a1481b7a-1e42-5a57-8bc2-c55fcac02ccb','bbe9aded-d3a7-5c00-a379-a9d03d3b8f21',4,null,null,'spoken & written','the way in which you are related to someone in your family','[ uncountable ]',null,'روشی که از طریق آن با یکی از اعضای خانواده خود در ارتباط هستید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"‘What’s your relationship to Sue?’ ‘She’s my cousin.’","translation":"\"رابطه شما با سو چیست؟\" \"او پسر عموی من است.\"","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652694.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('2e66d2f1-97c0-5062-8a60-ede1f2c106ae','7744f4a8-c6d2-5d4e-b52d-63ed98051079',1,null,null,'spoken & written','in the same order as the things you have just mentioned',null,null,'به‌ترتیب، به همین ترتیب؛ جداگانه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The cups and saucers cost £5 and £3 respectively.","translation":"قیمت فنجان ها و نعلبکی ها به ترتیب 5 پوند و 3 پوند است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000745783.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('11974505-992e-5e1b-b2a7-a61eedd8badb','be12db0b-8ea0-586e-ab31-ec96fb8bb018',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a feeling of happiness or pleasure because you have achieved something or got what you wanted','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'رضایت، خشنودی؛ رضایت (کار)؛ رضایت (سپری)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['great/deep satisfaction It was hard work, but it gave her great satisfaction.','immense/enormous satisfaction (= very great ) The victory gave him immense satisfaction.','real satisfaction (= great satisfaction ) There is real satisfaction in helping other people to overcome their problems.','complete satisfaction They expressed complete satisfaction with the agreement.','personal satisfaction (= happiness with your own life or achievements ) The job offered William little personal satisfaction.','quiet satisfaction (= satisfaction that you express in a quiet, not very obvious way ) He announced with quiet satisfaction that they had achieved their target.','grim satisfaction (= when you succeed or are proved right, but do not really feel happy about it ) ‘That’s exactly what I expected, ’ he said with grim satisfaction.','job satisfaction (= enjoyment of your job ) In general, job satisfaction among farm workers is extraordinarily high.','customer/patient/voter etc satisfaction (= among customers/patients/voters etc ) Staff work as a team to achieve customer satisfaction.','get satisfaction from something ( also gain/derive satisfaction from something formal ) I get a lot of satisfaction from teaching. He derived great satisfaction from knowing his son had followed in his footsteps.','find satisfaction in something They found satisfaction in helping others achieve their goals.','take satisfaction in/from something He took great satisfaction in doing his job well.','have the satisfaction of doing something They have the satisfaction of knowing that the company needs them.','something gives/brings somebody satisfaction To have won both awards in the same year gives us great satisfaction. Yet children also bring immense rewards and satisfaction.','feel satisfaction As she looked at what she had created, she felt a quiet satisfaction.','express satisfaction Those taking part expressed their satisfaction with the outcome of the talks.','a sense/feeling of satisfaction Performing such a difficult piece gave her a deep sense of satisfaction.','a smile/sigh/look of satisfaction He allowed himself a little smile of satisfaction.','the level of satisfaction (= the number of people who feel satisfied ) Research shows a high level of satisfaction with the system.','a source of satisfaction (= something that gives you a feeling of satisfaction ) It is a source of deep satisfaction to him that he was eventually proved to be right.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She got great satisfaction from helping people to learn.","translation":"او از کمک به مردم برای یادگیری رضایت زیادی کسب کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001918884.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘I’ve passed all my exams, ’ he announced with satisfaction.","translation":"او با رضایت اعلام کرد: من تمام امتحاناتم را پس داده ام.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001918901.mp3"},{"sentence":"Finance officials expressed satisfaction with the recovery of the dollar.","translation":"مقامات مالی از بهبود قیمت دلار ابراز خرسندی کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001918918.mp3"},{"sentence":"I didn''t want to give him the satisfaction of knowing that I was jealous.","translation":"نمی خواستم این رضایت را به او بدهم که بداند حسادت می کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040192.mp3"},{"sentence":"For her own satisfaction, she checked through the figures again.","translation":"برای رضایت خودش، دوباره ارقام را بررسی کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040193.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('f857df49-1e83-59fb-9809-1ceb065ebbf9','be12db0b-8ea0-586e-ab31-ec96fb8bb018',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'to somebody’s satisfaction','رضایت، خشنودی؛ رضایت (کار)؛ رضایت (سپری)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['great/deep satisfaction It was hard work, but it gave her great satisfaction.','immense/enormous satisfaction (= very great ) The victory gave him immense satisfaction.','real satisfaction (= great satisfaction ) There is real satisfaction in helping other people to overcome their problems.','complete satisfaction They expressed complete satisfaction with the agreement.','personal satisfaction (= happiness with your own life or achievements ) The job offered William little personal satisfaction.','quiet satisfaction (= satisfaction that you express in a quiet, not very obvious way ) He announced with quiet satisfaction that they had achieved their target.','grim satisfaction (= when you succeed or are proved right, but do not really feel happy about it ) ‘That’s exactly what I expected, ’ he said with grim satisfaction.','job satisfaction (= enjoyment of your job ) In general, job satisfaction among farm workers is extraordinarily high.','customer/patient/voter etc satisfaction (= among customers/patients/voters etc ) Staff work as a team to achieve customer satisfaction.','get satisfaction from something ( also gain/derive satisfaction from something formal ) I get a lot of satisfaction from teaching. He derived great satisfaction from knowing his son had followed in his footsteps.','find satisfaction in something They found satisfaction in helping others achieve their goals.','take satisfaction in/from something He took great satisfaction in doing his job well.','have the satisfaction of doing something They have the satisfaction of knowing that the company needs them.','something gives/brings somebody satisfaction To have won both awards in the same year gives us great satisfaction. Yet children also bring immense rewards and satisfaction.','feel satisfaction As she looked at what she had created, she felt a quiet satisfaction.','express satisfaction Those taking part expressed their satisfaction with the outcome of the talks.','a sense/feeling of satisfaction Performing such a difficult piece gave her a deep sense of satisfaction.','a smile/sigh/look of satisfaction He allowed himself a little smile of satisfaction.','the level of satisfaction (= the number of people who feel satisfied ) Research shows a high level of satisfaction with the system.','a source of satisfaction (= something that gives you a feeling of satisfaction ) It is a source of deep satisfaction to him that he was eventually proved to be right.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('06c4a63e-4ed8-52d2-800b-3e538b243c81','be12db0b-8ea0-586e-ab31-ec96fb8bb018',3,null,null,'spoken & written','when you get money or an apology from someone who has treated you badly or unfairly','[ uncountable ]',null,'وقتی از کسی که با شما بد یا ناعادلانه رفتار کرده است پول می گیرید یا عذرخواهی می کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['great/deep satisfaction It was hard work, but it gave her great satisfaction.','immense/enormous satisfaction (= very great ) The victory gave him immense satisfaction.','real satisfaction (= great satisfaction ) There is real satisfaction in helping other people to overcome their problems.','complete satisfaction They expressed complete satisfaction with the agreement.','personal satisfaction (= happiness with your own life or achievements ) The job offered William little personal satisfaction.','quiet satisfaction (= satisfaction that you express in a quiet, not very obvious way ) He announced with quiet satisfaction that they had achieved their target.','grim satisfaction (= when you succeed or are proved right, but do not really feel happy about it ) ‘That’s exactly what I expected, ’ he said with grim satisfaction.','job satisfaction (= enjoyment of your job ) In general, job satisfaction among farm workers is extraordinarily high.','customer/patient/voter etc satisfaction (= among customers/patients/voters etc ) Staff work as a team to achieve customer satisfaction.','get satisfaction from something ( also gain/derive satisfaction from something formal ) I get a lot of satisfaction from teaching. He derived great satisfaction from knowing his son had followed in his footsteps.','find satisfaction in something They found satisfaction in helping others achieve their goals.','take satisfaction in/from something He took great satisfaction in doing his job well.','have the satisfaction of doing something They have the satisfaction of knowing that the company needs them.','something gives/brings somebody satisfaction To have won both awards in the same year gives us great satisfaction. Yet children also bring immense rewards and satisfaction.','feel satisfaction As she looked at what she had created, she felt a quiet satisfaction.','express satisfaction Those taking part expressed their satisfaction with the outcome of the talks.','a sense/feeling of satisfaction Performing such a difficult piece gave her a deep sense of satisfaction.','a smile/sigh/look of satisfaction He allowed himself a little smile of satisfaction.','the level of satisfaction (= the number of people who feel satisfied ) Research shows a high level of satisfaction with the system.','a source of satisfaction (= something that gives you a feeling of satisfaction ) It is a source of deep satisfaction to him that he was eventually proved to be right.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I got no satisfaction from the customer complaints department.","translation":"من از بخش شکایات مشتریان رضایت نداشتم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634086.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('1723e4a4-8099-5a82-90bf-f83b13932c17','be12db0b-8ea0-586e-ab31-ec96fb8bb018',4,null,null,'formal','when someone gets something that they want, need, or have demanded','[ uncountable ]',null,'وقتی کسی چیزی را بدست می آورد که می خواهد، نیاز دارد یا خواسته است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['great/deep satisfaction It was hard work, but it gave her great satisfaction.','immense/enormous satisfaction (= very great ) The victory gave him immense satisfaction.','real satisfaction (= great satisfaction ) There is real satisfaction in helping other people to overcome their problems.','complete satisfaction They expressed complete satisfaction with the agreement.','personal satisfaction (= happiness with your own life or achievements ) The job offered William little personal satisfaction.','quiet satisfaction (= satisfaction that you express in a quiet, not very obvious way ) He announced with quiet satisfaction that they had achieved their target.','grim satisfaction (= when you succeed or are proved right, but do not really feel happy about it ) ‘That’s exactly what I expected, ’ he said with grim satisfaction.','job satisfaction (= enjoyment of your job ) In general, job satisfaction among farm workers is extraordinarily high.','customer/patient/voter etc satisfaction (= among customers/patients/voters etc ) Staff work as a team to achieve customer satisfaction.','get satisfaction from something ( also gain/derive satisfaction from something formal ) I get a lot of satisfaction from teaching. He derived great satisfaction from knowing his son had followed in his footsteps.','find satisfaction in something They found satisfaction in helping others achieve their goals.','take satisfaction in/from something He took great satisfaction in doing his job well.','have the satisfaction of doing something They have the satisfaction of knowing that the company needs them.','something gives/brings somebody satisfaction To have won both awards in the same year gives us great satisfaction. Yet children also bring immense rewards and satisfaction.','feel satisfaction As she looked at what she had created, she felt a quiet satisfaction.','express satisfaction Those taking part expressed their satisfaction with the outcome of the talks.','a sense/feeling of satisfaction Performing such a difficult piece gave her a deep sense of satisfaction.','a smile/sigh/look of satisfaction He allowed himself a little smile of satisfaction.','the level of satisfaction (= the number of people who feel satisfied ) Research shows a high level of satisfaction with the system.','a source of satisfaction (= something that gives you a feeling of satisfaction ) It is a source of deep satisfaction to him that he was eventually proved to be right.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the satisfaction of basic human needs","translation":"ارضای نیازهای اساسی انسان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000714475.mp3"},{"sentence":"sexual satisfaction","translation":"رضایت جنسی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000714476.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('f9d5a4f4-3c8d-50dc-8100-c7f9f0b5c861','c6225a86-2901-5587-9a95-e818ea4a2877',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the importance of an event, action etc, especially because of the effects or influence it will have in the future',null,null,'اهمیت، اهمیت (رخداد)؛ اهمیت (نتایج)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['great/considerable significance The judge said the new evidence was of great significance.','little significance This information on its own is of little significance.','wider significance The research dealt with one small group, but their conclusions are of much wider significance.','special significance This place has a special significance for Icelanders.','political/social/historical etc significance The political significance of this change should not be underestimated.','have significance A child''s relationship to his parents has a lasting significance for his future relationships.','attach significance to something (= give something importance ) They say they don''t attach much significance to opinion polls.','take on a new/special etc significance (= start to have it ) Sporting competitions took on a new political significance during the Cold War.','acquire/assume significance formal (= take on significance ) As links with Europe continue to grow, language learning assumes even greater significance.','grasp/appreciate/understand the significance of something The press was slow to grasp the significance of what had happened.','assess the significance of something (= decide how important something is ) It is often difficult to assess the significance of an event until more time has passed.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Stella didn’t attach any significance to Doug’s query.","translation":"استلا هیچ اهمیتی به درخواست داگ نداد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001672746.mp3"},{"sentence":"the significance of climate change","translation":"اهمیت تغییر آب و هوا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000685484.mp3"},{"sentence":"The book assesses the significance of Stalin’s policies between 1927 and 1939.","translation":"این کتاب اهمیت سیاست های استالین را بین سال های 1927 و 1939 ارزیابی می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000685475.mp3"},{"sentence":"The results of the study have a wider significance for all the profession.","translation":"نتایج مطالعه از اهمیت گسترده تری برای همه حرفه ها برخوردار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001672752.mp3"},{"sentence":"The crime problem has great significance to the general public.","translation":"مشکل جرم و جنایت برای عموم مردم اهمیت زیادی دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001672755.mp3"},{"sentence":"The press were slow to grasp the significance of what happened.","translation":"مطبوعات در درک اهمیت آنچه اتفاق افتاد دیر بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001672762.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('ca4ee01a-a5a8-532e-83f5-75463276061c','c6225a86-2901-5587-9a95-e818ea4a2877',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the meaning of a word, sign, action etc, especially when this is not immediately clear',null,null,'معنی یک کلمه، علامت، عمل و غیره، به ویژه زمانی که این بلافاصله روشن نیست','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['great/considerable significance The judge said the new evidence was of great significance.','little significance This information on its own is of little significance.','wider significance The research dealt with one small group, but their conclusions are of much wider significance.','special significance This place has a special significance for Icelanders.','political/social/historical etc significance The political significance of this change should not be underestimated.','have significance A child''s relationship to his parents has a lasting significance for his future relationships.','attach significance to something (= give something importance ) They say they don''t attach much significance to opinion polls.','take on a new/special etc significance (= start to have it ) Sporting competitions took on a new political significance during the Cold War.','acquire/assume significance formal (= take on significance ) As links with Europe continue to grow, language learning assumes even greater significance.','grasp/appreciate/understand the significance of something The press was slow to grasp the significance of what had happened.','assess the significance of something (= decide how important something is ) It is often difficult to assess the significance of an event until more time has passed.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the significance of the words that refer to the bread Christ shares with his disciples","translation":"اهمیت کلماتی که به نانی که مسیح با شاگردانش به اشتراک می گذارد، اشاره دارد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001775204.mp3"},{"sentence":"Only later did we realize the true significance of his remark.","translation":"فقط بعداً به اهمیت واقعی سخنان او پی بردیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000685478.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('2a7717b1-5012-5e48-a085-9dc7460f1d3f','a128f81a-8721-5156-ab56-c9fa0d63995f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','relating to or intended for one particular type of person or thing only',null,null,'به‌طور خاص، مخصوصاً؛ ویژه (کار)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"advertising that specifically targets children","translation":"تبلیغاتی که به طور خاص کودکان را هدف قرار می دهد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000655671.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('28b675b0-7aa7-5828-aad0-8f7117959cac','a128f81a-8721-5156-ab56-c9fa0d63995f',2,null,null,'spoken & written','in a detailed or exact way',null,null,'به صورت دقیق یا دقیق','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I specifically asked you not to do that!","translation":"من به طور خاص از شما خواستم که این کار را نکنید!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000655675.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('a8ca1bf0-7143-5a46-948a-754fa7b53060','a128f81a-8721-5156-ab56-c9fa0d63995f',3,null,null,'spoken & written','used when you are adding more exact information','[ sentence adverb ]',null,'زمانی استفاده می شود که اطلاعات دقیق تری را اضافه می کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Specifically, the department wanted answers to the following questions.","translation":"به طور خاص، بخش پاسخ به سؤالات زیر را می خواست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000655680.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('488218cd-e206-5e46-80c0-f56f62563c79','7b4f4370-eeb9-5cc6-834e-66875f1144e3',1,null,null,'spoken & written','after an event in the past',null,null,'بعداً، پس از آن؛ سپس','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The book was subsequently translated into 15 languages.","translation":"این کتاب پس از آن به 15 زبان ترجمه شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000626476.mp3"},{"sentence":"Subsequently, the company filed for bankruptcy.","translation":"متعاقباً این شرکت اعلام ورشکستگی کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001742946.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('619f6024-54f6-51ec-89ec-cfff8e49865d','f8d65717-f0cf-5b10-b137-421c938bd292',1,null,null,'spoken & written','unusually or unexpectedly',null,null,'به‌طور شگفت‌آور، غیرمنتظره؛ عجیب','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The exam was surprisingly easy.","translation":"امتحان به طرز شگفت آوری آسان بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000956737.mp3"},{"sentence":"Not surprisingly , with youth unemployment so high, some school-leavers with qualifications fail to find jobs.","translation":"جای تعجب نیست که با افزایش بیکاری جوانان، برخی از فارغ التحصیلان با شرایط تحصیلی موفق به یافتن شغل نمی شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000956741.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('f1d80a3a-13cc-5ec9-a623-f775421bc7eb','f76e9d9f-55db-55a1-8ff7-36f08ebc2c17',1,null,null,'spoken & written','very good, successful , or impressive',null,null,'باورنکردنی، حیرت‌انگیز؛ باورنکردنی (فرد)',array['amazing']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The opportunities are unbelievable.","translation":"فرصت ها باور نکردنی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001617737.mp3"},{"sentence":"an unbelievable talent","translation":"یک استعداد باور نکردنی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001617738.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('47e1d9b0-95a7-515f-bd1e-649bf499dff7','f76e9d9f-55db-55a1-8ff7-36f08ebc2c17',2,null,null,'spoken & written','very bad or shocking',null,null,'خیلی بد یا تکان دهنده',array['terrible']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The pain was unbelievable.","translation":"درد غیر قابل باور بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001617744.mp3"},{"sentence":"acts of unbelievable cruelty","translation":"اعمال ظالمانه باور نکردنی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001617745.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was unbelievable that we were expected to pay twice.","translation":"باور نکردنی بود که از ما انتظار دوبار پرداخت می شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001617746.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('9e688a20-be23-5ed1-8444-4eaa7192ebb3','f76e9d9f-55db-55a1-8ff7-36f08ebc2c17',3,null,null,'spoken & written','so extreme that it hardly seems possible',null,null,'آنقدر افراطی که به سختی ممکن به نظر می رسد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He’s so lazy it’s unbelievable.","translation":"او آنقدر تنبل است که باور نکردنی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001617754.mp3"},{"sentence":"an unbelievable speed","translation":"سرعتی باور نکردنی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001617755.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('a458337a-7165-55b6-aed0-1228a71b97bb','f76e9d9f-55db-55a1-8ff7-36f08ebc2c17',4,null,null,'spoken & written','very difficult to believe and therefore probably untrue',null,null,'باور کردن بسیار دشوار است و بنابراین احتمالاً نادرست است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Yvonne’s excuse for being late was totally unbelievable.","translation":"بهانه ایوون برای دیر رسیدن کاملاً باورنکردنی بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000544845.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('ce7092ef-fc4e-551c-876c-4f740eba299a','8cba08a1-7759-5019-8f74-c5da099f96fd',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the number of people in a particular country or area who cannot get a job',null,null,'بیکاری، بی‌کاری؛ بیکاری (نرخ)؛ بیکاری (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['high They live in an area where unemployment is high.','low The area has the lowest unemployment in Europe.','rising/falling unemployment Rising unemployment led to more crime.','mass unemployment (= when very large numbers of people are unemployed ) the mass unemployment of the 1930s','long-term unemployment (= when people are unemployed for a long period of time ) It can be difficult to help people out of long-term unemployment.','large-scale unemployment (= when a lot of people are unemployed ) Large-scale unemployment among young people could have terrible social consequences.','massive unemployment These measures could result in massive unemployment in the construction industry.','serious/severe unemployment After the pit closed, the town experienced severe unemployment.','widespread unemployment (= in many places ) The collapse of the currency led to widespread unemployment.','youth/male/female unemployment (= the number of young people/men/women unemployed ) Youth unemployment there has reached 50 percent.','reduce/cut/bring down unemployment The government is spending more on projects to cut unemployment.','cause unemployment People blamed immigrants for causing unemployment.','combat/fight unemployment The government’s first priority is to combat unemployment.','unemployment increases/rises During their term in office unemployment increased by 50 percent.','unemployment soars (= increases quickly to a high level ) The economic crisis has seen unemployment soar.','a rise/increase in unemployment The crisis meant a sharp rise in unemployment.','a fall/reduction in unemployment We are hoping to see a fall in unemployment.','the unemployment rate The unemployment rate was 17 percent.','the unemployment level The unemployment level among young people is rising.','unemployment figures/statistics They publish monthly unemployment figures for the UK.','an unemployment blackspot British English (= an area where there is higher unemployment than in other places ) The town became an unemployment blackspot after the factory closure.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a town where there is high unemployment","translation":"شهری که در آن بیکاری بالاست","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001667.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('cb7f4a33-01d1-584b-bd23-0c7b7112ba54','8cba08a1-7759-5019-8f74-c5da099f96fd',2,null,null,'spoken & written','when someone does not have a job',null,null,'وقتی کسی شغل ندارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['high They live in an area where unemployment is high.','low The area has the lowest unemployment in Europe.','rising/falling unemployment Rising unemployment led to more crime.','mass unemployment (= when very large numbers of people are unemployed ) the mass unemployment of the 1930s','long-term unemployment (= when people are unemployed for a long period of time ) It can be difficult to help people out of long-term unemployment.','large-scale unemployment (= when a lot of people are unemployed ) Large-scale unemployment among young people could have terrible social consequences.','massive unemployment These measures could result in massive unemployment in the construction industry.','serious/severe unemployment After the pit closed, the town experienced severe unemployment.','widespread unemployment (= in many places ) The collapse of the currency led to widespread unemployment.','youth/male/female unemployment (= the number of young people/men/women unemployed ) Youth unemployment there has reached 50 percent.','reduce/cut/bring down unemployment The government is spending more on projects to cut unemployment.','cause unemployment People blamed immigrants for causing unemployment.','combat/fight unemployment The government’s first priority is to combat unemployment.','unemployment increases/rises During their term in office unemployment increased by 50 percent.','unemployment soars (= increases quickly to a high level ) The economic crisis has seen unemployment soar.','a rise/increase in unemployment The crisis meant a sharp rise in unemployment.','a fall/reduction in unemployment We are hoping to see a fall in unemployment.','the unemployment rate The unemployment rate was 17 percent.','the unemployment level The unemployment level among young people is rising.','unemployment figures/statistics They publish monthly unemployment figures for the UK.','an unemployment blackspot British English (= an area where there is higher unemployment than in other places ) The town became an unemployment blackspot after the factory closure.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Closure of the plant means 80 workers are facing unemployment.","translation":"تعطیلی این کارخانه به معنای بیکاری 80 کارگر است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000549019.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
